  "transcript": "He steals $100 from the cash register, then walks away, slipping it into his pocket. The next day, he goes back to the same store and picks up $70 worth of candy, using that same $100 bill to pay, and the cashier hands him $30 in change. So how much did the store actually lose? Well, some people add the original $100, plus the $70 worth of candy and the $30 in change, making a total loss of $200. But that would be counting it twice, since he gave back the stolen $100 bill when he paid. So in the end, the store only lost two things, the $70 worth of candy and the $30 in change, meaning the total loss was exactly $100.",
